Hi,

A packaging progress update for this ITP: the conventional Debian source
package is now available, version 0.4.0+20261020-0exp1, proposed initially
for experimental/contrib. The existing RFS is #1151425:

https://bugs.debian.org/1151425

Signed source files, build provenance and review evidence:
https://github.com/rdmitry0911/qsm-rd/releases/tag/v0.4.0-debian-contrib-20261020-review2

The October 20 validation includes unprivileged builds with networking
disabled on Debian 13 and unstable, 19 passing CTest tests in each build,
clean Lintian source/binary checks and a passing source-units autopkgtest
on unstable. Build dependencies are in Debian main; external Proxmox
packages remain runtime dependencies, which is why I propose contrib.

Independent human review and a Debian Developer upload sponsor are still
needed. The new debhelper maintainer-script integration also needs PVE
install/upgrade/removal review before an upload. No upload to the Debian
archive has taken place. AI assistance is disclosed in the original ITP,
RFS and source review material.

Thanks,
Dmitry
